# /full-deploy-light — Commit + push + merge in one shot (small projects)

The all-in-one "ship it" command for small projects. Combines `/wrapup-light`
(safety checks + commit) and `/deploy-light` (push + PR + squash-merge)
into a single invocation. Use this when you're done with a chunk of work
and want it on the base branch as fast as possible without ceremony.

If the tree is clean (no uncommitted changes), it still runs the deploy
half — useful when you have local commits that haven't been pushed yet.

If you ship a `.deploy-check.json` at the repo root, it's verified before
the push (catches "render exited 0 but produced no MP4" style silent
failures). If you don't ship one, the check skips silently.

This is the heaviest of the three "-light" commands — but still much
lighter than the framework `/wrapup` + `/remote-deploy` pipeline.

## Usage

- `/full-deploy-light` — default. Safety checks, commit, push, PR, squash-merge.
- `/full-deploy-light --lessons` — also prompt for a one-line lesson after commit.
- `/full-deploy-light --base <branch>` — override base branch (e.g. `--base develop`).
- `/full-deploy-light --no-pull` — skip pre-push rebase.
- `/full-deploy-light --force` — bypass safety check failures (use sparingly).

## What this skill will NOT do

- Run tests (none assumed)
- Update workflow logs, build orders, Content Library
- Sync to High Level Vibing
- Deploy to Vercel (use the heavy `/remote-deploy` for that)

## Process

### Step 1: Run the helper script

```bash
node ~/.claude/scripts/light-deploy.mjs full [flags...]
```

Pass through whichever flags the user supplied (`--lessons`, `--base`,
`--no-pull`, `--force`).

The script runs the wrapup half (safety checks + commit), then the deploy
half (push + PR + merge), and prints a single JSON object on stdout.

### Step 2: Interpret the JSON

The success payload has two nested blocks: `wrapup` and `deploy`. Both
will be present on success.

```json
{
  "ok": true,
  "action": "full",
  "wrapup": { "no_changes": false, "commit_sha": "abc1234", "files_committed": 5, "lessons_prompt": false },
  "deploy": { "pushed": true, "branch": "...", "pr_url": "...", "pr_number": 7, "merge_sha": "d1d3d5e", "branch_deleted": true }
}
```

Report a compact summary:

> "Committed `abc1234` (5 files) and merged [PR #7](url) — `d1d3d5e`."

If `wrapup.no_changes: true` (the tree was already clean), the wrapup half
was effectively a no-op and the deploy half handled any existing local
commits. Report accordingly:

> "Tree was clean. Pushed and merged [PR #7](url) — `d1d3d5e`."

If `deploy.pr` is `"skipped (on base branch)"` or
`"skipped (no commits ahead of base)"`, report that the push happened but
no PR was needed.

On **failure** (`ok: false`):

- The `stage` tells you which half failed — wrapup stages
  (`sensitive-files`, `secrets`, `large-files`, `zone-verification`,
  `commit`) or deploy stages (`dirty-tree`, `deploy-check`, `pull`,
  `push`, `pr-create`, `merge`).
- Surface the `error` field verbatim. Do NOT retry automatically.

### Step 3: Lessons-learned prompt (only if `wrapup.lessons_prompt: true`)

Only when the user passed `--lessons`. Follow the same flow as
`/wrapup-light`:

1. `AskUserQuestion`: "One-line lesson from this session? Pick 'Skip' to write nothing."
2. If user picks "Write a lesson," capture the next message as the lesson.
3. Append to `<project-root>/LESSONS.md` as `YYYY-MM-DD | <lesson>`.

### Step 4: Done

One-line summary. The PR URL is the most useful thing to surface.

## Error decoder (combined wrapup + deploy stages)

| `stage` | Where it failed | Action |
|---------|----------------|--------|
| `git-health` | Both halves use it | Surface verbatim |
| `sensitive-files` | Wrapup | Add to `.gitignore` or `--force` |
| `large-files` | Wrapup | Use Git LFS or `--force` |
| `secrets` | Wrapup | Remove the secret, then re-run |
| `zone-verification` | Wrapup (Windows + protection installed) | Fix TS errors |
| `commit` | Wrapup | Surface the git error |
| `deploy-check` | Deploy | Check the listed missing/undersized files |
| `pull` | Deploy | Resolve rebase conflicts manually |
| `push` | Deploy | Usually permissions or upstream conflict |
| `pr-create` | Deploy | `gh auth login`, ensure repo is on GitHub |
| `merge` | Deploy | Check branch protections, required reviews |

## Related commands

- `/wrapup-light` — just the commit half
- `/deploy-light` — just the push + merge half (requires pre-existing commit)
